MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_Fab_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_Fab_m01_001: It has been roughly five years since I first left\nFódlan and set foot upon this land.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_Fab_m01_002: I must admit that, until I met you, I had\naccomplished little in my wanderings.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_Fab_m01_003: Though I thought I had little attachment to\nthat place...
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_Fab_m01_004: oddly I now feel a strange feeling of fondness for it\nwelling up in my breast.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_Fab_m01_005: *sigh* That I would feel this? Ridiculous!
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_Fab_m01_006: Grrr... Yes! This gently constrictive sensation in my\nchest! It is truly wonderful!
MID_LGA_1DIT_c07_Fab_m01: <BLN>Strange...
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_Esm_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_Esm_m01_001: Lake Baal spreads out like the sea, but it's actually\na freshwater lake, right?
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_Esm_m01_002: I wonder if that's why all the fish they catch in\nDagsion smell strange.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_Esm_m01_003: Truth is, the fish you can catch off the coast of Fina\nreally do taste the best.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_Esm_m01_004: *sigh* Think that just means I'm starting to miss\nFina. A little bit. But I'm OK.
MID_LGA_1DIT_c07_Esm_m01: <BLN>Maybe I do miss Fina.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_Mic_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_Mic_m01_001: I wonder why the Twin Jewels of Arago showed up\nin Dagsion...
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_Mic_m01_002: Dietrich, did you do something to incur the wrath of\nthe king of Arago?
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_Mic_m01_003: Wait...it's me they're after. No! It can't be... Can it?
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_Mic_m01_004: Sure, I did what I had to. I had to escape that mine!\nBut this...this is excessive!
MID_LGA_1DIT_c07_Mic_m01: <BLN>There's no way! There just isn't!
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_Hri_Nat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_Hri_Nat_m01_001: Things are getting out of hand. So much so that our\nlovely chancellor might lose her grip on them.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_Hri_Nat_m01_002: I wonder what she has against that priest in the\ncat mask.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_Hri_Nat_m01_003: Hold, Creek. We're not alone.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_Hri_Nat_m01_004: Sorry, but we're busy, friend. If you have business,\ncome back later.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_Hri_Nat_m01_005: Don't be so hasty, Nathan. This is the swordsman in\nblack—the talk of the town.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_Hri_Nat_m01_006: See that grotesque sword? Rumor has it he crossed\nthe seas to reach this land.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_Hri_Nat_m01_007: Dietrich of House Lamine, is it?
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_Hri_Nat_m01_008: You're our next opponent, then. I look forward to\nour fight.
MID_LGA_1DIT_c07_Nat_m01: <BLN>Nothing good will come of this.
MID_LGA_1DIT_c07_Hri_m01: <BLN>I, for one, am fascinated.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_Set_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_Set_m01_001: Your next foes seem to be quite celebrated\nacross this land.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_Set_m01_002: I'll be observing what you can do.
MID_LGA_1DIT_c07_Set_m01: <BLN>Show me what you can do.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_B01_m01_001: It seems your next opponents are very well-known...
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_B01_m01_002: I will visit the temple of Mars and pray for\nyour victory!
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_B01_m01_003: For now, there is this. Please take it.
MID_LGA_1DIT_c07_B01_m01: <BLN>I pray for your victory.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_B02_m01_001: Never thought I'd witness the Twin Jewels of Arago\nfight with my own two eyes!
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_B02_m01_002: I don't care if I have to beg off work—I've got to see\nthis next match!
MID_LGA_1DIT_c07_B02_m01: <BLN>There's no way I'm missing this.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_B03_m01_001: Twin Jewels of Arago... You've heard of them, right?\nThey're the bravest and strongest knights EVER!
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_B03_m01_002: Nathan, the Catoblepas, is strong enough to lift\na horse!
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_B03_m01_003: Creek, the Pantere, is as swift as a leopard and\nsmarter than, well, anybody!
MID_LGA_1DIT_c07_B03_m01: <BLN>They're the best!
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_B04_m01_001: Nathan...and Creek... So wonderful.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_B04_m01_002: Perhaps you've heard that the king and queen of\nArago are to be guests of honor at the next match.
MID_LGV_1DIT_c07_B04_m01_003: The Twin Jewels accompanied them to Dagsion as\ntheir bodyguards!
MID_LGA_1DIT_c07_B04_m01: <BLN>How wonderful!